WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.779
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute Papers
with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.779 --> 00:00:13.700
Today we are going to see how OpenAI’s DALL-E
2 AI’s images stack up to real works from

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:14.700
real artists.

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:20.310
This is going to be an amazing journey, so,
hold on tight to your papers!

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:25.320
DALL-E 2 is an AI that took the world by storm
in the last few months.

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:27.150
What does it do?

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:33.590
Well, we can write it a text description,
and hand it to the AI that creates an amazing

00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:35.980
image of exactly that.

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:40.630
And now, I am lucky to say that, yes, I have
ascended!

00:00:40.630 --> 00:00:46.720
Thanks to the generosity of OpenAI, I now
have access to DALL-E 2.

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:53.410
And my first thought was, that if it can come
up with high-quality, and truly novel images,

00:00:53.410 --> 00:00:56.070
let’s put those to the real test.

00:00:56.070 --> 00:01:01.520
In other words, see how they stand up against
the works of real artists.

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:08.680
Our first subject will be my favorite artist
in the world, and that would be my wife, Felícia

00:01:08.680 --> 00:01:09.680
Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:11.580
She drew this chimpanzee.

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:14.390
Oh my, that is beautiful.

00:01:14.390 --> 00:01:18.340
So, let’s try this against DALL-E 2.

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:20.750
Okay, but how?

00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:26.620
Well, the first way of trying it will be through
variant generation.

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:27.680
What is that?

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:34.711
Well, since this AI is trained to understand
the connection between text and images, the

00:01:34.711 --> 00:01:38.030
understanding goes both ways.

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:44.500
This means that we can not only input text
and get an image, but input an image too.

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:47.590
Does it understand what is depicted in this
image?

00:01:47.590 --> 00:01:49.030
Let’s see.

00:01:49.030 --> 00:01:50.470
Oh yes.

00:01:50.470 --> 00:01:57.690
Wow, it not only understands what is going
on, but it can demonstrate that by creating

00:01:57.690 --> 00:01:59.740
really good variants of it.

00:01:59.740 --> 00:02:03.440
But, not nearly as good as Felícia, I have
to say.

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:05.530
Let’s give it another chance.

00:02:05.530 --> 00:02:11.750
Here, I used a text prompt to get a hand-drawn
chimp looking to the right.

00:02:11.750 --> 00:02:14.630
And I asked for lots and lots of detail.

00:02:14.630 --> 00:02:21.200
I’ve pleaded and pleaded for extra wrinkles
to squeeze everything out of the AI, even

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:25.290
cherrypicked the results, and these were the
best I could get.

00:02:25.290 --> 00:02:30.280
You know, art is highly subjective, that’s
what makes it what it is.

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:35.540
But for now, I have to say Team Humanity,
team AI, 1-0.

00:02:35.540 --> 00:02:41.020
At this point, I thought this is going to
be easy.

00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:42.830
Easy easy easy.

00:02:42.830 --> 00:02:47.040
And boy, you’ll find out in a moment how
wrong I was.

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:53.170
Here is a work from one of my other favorite
artists, Judit Somogyvári.

00:02:53.170 --> 00:02:54.170
Wow.

00:02:54.170 --> 00:02:59.720
That is one of her original characters, very
imaginative, I love it.

00:02:59.720 --> 00:03:03.140
So, let’s ask for a variant of that.

00:03:03.140 --> 00:03:06.090
Does the AI understand what is going on?

00:03:06.090 --> 00:03:12.420
You know, there is a lot to take in here,
elf ears, make up, and the…wow.

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:14.420
I cannot believe that.

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:19.740
I am lucky that the variants are working out
so well, because writing a prompt for this

00:03:19.740 --> 00:03:21.670
would be a bit of a challenge.

00:03:21.670 --> 00:03:24.640
I am truly out of words.

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:26.030
These are so good.

00:03:26.030 --> 00:03:30.300
But, not as good as Judit, in my opinion.

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:33.129
Team Humanity vs Team AI, 2-0.

00:03:33.129 --> 00:03:36.600
That’s a good score, but it is getting harder.

00:03:36.600 --> 00:03:40.819
Now, let’s look at one of Judit’s other
works.

00:03:40.819 --> 00:03:44.980
An ostrich that is also a formula one racer.

00:03:44.980 --> 00:03:49.720
I am loving this, especially the helmet and
the goggles.

00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:52.959
I think I can whip up a good prompt for this.

00:03:52.959 --> 00:03:56.790
So, what did the AI come up with?

00:03:56.790 --> 00:03:58.790
Holy mother of papers!

00:03:58.790 --> 00:04:00.129
Is this some kind of joke?

00:04:00.129 --> 00:04:02.120
It cannot be that good.

00:04:02.120 --> 00:04:05.300
I checked the images over and over again.

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:06.810
It is that good.

00:04:06.810 --> 00:04:07.810
Wow.

00:04:07.810 --> 00:04:13.470
Now, of course, scoring this is subjective,
but clearly, both are excellent.

00:04:13.470 --> 00:04:16.090
I’ll give this one a tie.

00:04:16.090 --> 00:04:18.840
Team Humanity vs Team AI, 3-1.

00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:22.740
I told you, it is getting harder.

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:28.400
Make sure to check out both Judit, and Felícia’s
works, the links are available in the video

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:29.490
description.

00:04:29.490 --> 00:04:36.150
And now, for the next test, please give a
warm welcome to the King of All Donuts.

00:04:36.150 --> 00:04:42.340
Of course, that is the great Andrew Price,
3d modeler and teacher extraordinaire.

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:47.870
Now, here are some of the donuts I came up
with using DALL-E 2.

00:04:47.870 --> 00:04:51.889
And some from the prompts that I ran for my
daughter.

00:04:51.889 --> 00:04:54.219
Loving the googly eyes there, by the way.

00:04:54.219 --> 00:04:56.620
So, these are some great donuts.

00:04:56.620 --> 00:05:00.370
Now, Andrew, it’s your turn.

00:05:00.370 --> 00:05:07.180
Let’s see…wow OpenAI’s was a good one,
but this, this is a Michelin-star donut right

00:05:07.180 --> 00:05:08.180
there.

00:05:08.180 --> 00:05:11.340
The AI-made ones are no match for Andrew’s
skills.

00:05:11.340 --> 00:05:15.919
So, Team Humanity vs Team AI, 4-1.

00:05:15.919 --> 00:05:22.900
Note that DALL-E 2 often isn’t as good as
a real, world-class artist, but the AI can

00:05:22.900 --> 00:05:26.840
create 10000 of these images a day.

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:30.349
That must be worth at least a point.

00:05:30.349 --> 00:05:32.050
So, 4-2.

00:05:32.050 --> 00:05:33.050
Whew!

00:05:33.050 --> 00:05:34.050
We made it.

00:05:34.050 --> 00:05:40.030
Now, all this testing is great fun, and of
course, highly subjective, so don’t take

00:05:40.030 --> 00:05:41.789
it too seriously.

00:05:41.789 --> 00:05:44.889
And here comes the even more important lesson.

00:05:44.889 --> 00:05:51.729
In my opinion, this tool should not be framed
at all as Team Humanity versus Team AI.

00:05:51.729 --> 00:05:57.430
I believe this should be framed as Team Humanity,
supercharged by Team AI.

00:05:57.430 --> 00:06:01.090
Here’s why through 6 inspiring examples.

00:06:01.090 --> 00:06:02.090
Look.

00:06:02.090 --> 00:06:09.089
First, this is my second favorite prompt ever,
a grumpy cat in a spaceship.

00:06:09.089 --> 00:06:10.569
That is incredible.

00:06:10.569 --> 00:06:18.059
Now, almost as soon as I posted it on Twitter,
it inspired Fabian to create an animated version

00:06:18.059 --> 00:06:19.059
of it.

00:06:19.059 --> 00:06:23.349
And now, our adorable little Grump is ready
for takeoff.

00:06:23.349 --> 00:06:28.379
Through the ingenuity of Team Human and Team
AI together.

00:06:28.379 --> 00:06:29.669
So cool!

00:06:29.669 --> 00:06:31.199
What a time to be alive!

00:06:31.199 --> 00:06:36.839
So, I hear you asking, if this was my second
favorite, what is the first?

00:06:36.839 --> 00:06:40.649
Well, two, have a look at this fox scientist.

00:06:40.649 --> 00:06:45.009
I cannot believe how well this came out.

00:06:45.009 --> 00:06:47.180
It has tons of personality.

00:06:47.180 --> 00:06:51.720
And, it also inspired others to repaint it.

00:06:51.720 --> 00:06:52.720
Here it is.

00:06:52.720 --> 00:06:56.139
You see, I don’t see this as a competition.

00:06:56.139 --> 00:06:58.379
I see this as collaboration.

00:06:58.379 --> 00:07:05.429
Three, it also inspired the great beardyman,
who wanted to see a platypus studying the

00:07:05.429 --> 00:07:09.389
schematics for a cold fusion reactor.

00:07:09.389 --> 00:07:15.930
These are absolutely amazing, not just the
quality, but the variety of the results.

00:07:15.930 --> 00:07:17.199
My goodness.

00:07:17.199 --> 00:07:23.360
Note that he asked for a one-eyed platypus,
but this iteration of DALL-E is not that good

00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:24.800
with numbers.

00:07:24.800 --> 00:07:25.800
Yet.

00:07:25.800 --> 00:07:28.749
If it could talk, it would probably apologize
for it.

00:07:28.749 --> 00:07:35.289
Four, I also ran a prompt for David Brown
from Boyinaband which got real interesting

00:07:35.289 --> 00:07:36.419
real quick.

00:07:36.419 --> 00:07:39.240
He was looking for a visual pun.

00:07:39.240 --> 00:07:40.559
What is that?

00:07:40.559 --> 00:07:42.179
Is this a pan?

00:07:42.179 --> 00:07:45.139
Is this the pun, that we got a pan instead?

00:07:45.139 --> 00:07:49.939
I am not sure, but this is very cool nonetheless.

00:07:49.939 --> 00:07:53.959
And I also wonder what the AI is trying to
say here.

00:07:53.959 --> 00:07:58.899
Five, James from Linus Tech Tips also ran
a superb prompt.

00:07:58.899 --> 00:08:03.569
A time traveler insensitive to humanity's
trivialities.

00:08:03.569 --> 00:08:05.039
What a great idea!

00:08:05.039 --> 00:08:10.240
Oh my, loving the framing and the thoughtfulness
of these results.

00:08:10.240 --> 00:08:13.719
And finally, six, it inspired me too.

00:08:13.719 --> 00:08:16.020
I also made this.

00:08:16.020 --> 00:08:19.429
All hail the mighty Cyberfrog!

00:08:19.429 --> 00:08:20.569
Loving it.

00:08:20.569 --> 00:08:26.179
And we also have a tiny chihuahua in our home
and in the Two Minute Papers labs.

00:08:26.179 --> 00:08:29.379
She is Rosie, the paper dog, if you will.

00:08:29.379 --> 00:08:31.529
This is how we see her.

00:08:31.529 --> 00:08:37.330
And now, we can also show how she sees herself
when meeting other dogs.

00:08:37.330 --> 00:08:42.210
Oh yes, I think that is very accurate.

00:08:42.210 --> 00:08:45.630
And of course, as always, +1.

00:08:45.630 --> 00:08:50.940
You did not think we would leave without looking
at some of you Fellow Scholars holding on

00:08:50.940 --> 00:08:51.961
to your papers, did you?

00:08:51.961 --> 00:08:53.680
Here you go.

00:08:53.680 --> 00:08:58.690
And as you see, these are some proper papers.

00:08:58.690 --> 00:09:01.280
You Fellow Scholars are loving it.

00:09:01.280 --> 00:09:06.200
But now, let’s have an even more explosive
paper, like DALL-E 2.

00:09:06.200 --> 00:09:07.690
Oh yes!

00:09:07.690 --> 00:09:09.070
Now we are talking!

00:09:09.070 --> 00:09:14.620
This scholar is you, who knows that this paper
is history in the making.

00:09:14.620 --> 00:09:19.830
So much so that I cannot stop thinking about
and playing with this thing.

00:09:19.830 --> 00:09:22.200
It really keeps me up at night.

00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:27.220
This is an incredible achievement that is
going to transform the world around us.

00:09:27.220 --> 00:09:28.220
And fast.

00:09:28.220 --> 00:09:32.530
So, artists, AI people, what do you think?

00:09:32.530 --> 00:09:34.610
Which results did you like better?

00:09:34.610 --> 00:09:36.780
Let me know in the comments below!

00:09:36.780 --> 00:09:42.760
Also, I will be on Twitter taking some requests
from my followers, so make sure to follow

00:09:42.760 --> 00:09:45.250
us there and send some prompts!

00:09:45.250 --> 00:09:48.660
The best ones may appear in a future episode
here.

00:09:48.660 --> 00:10:28.960
The link 

00:10:28.960 --> 00:10:45.730
is in the description.

00:10:45.730 --> 00:10:49.110
Thanks for watching and for your generous
support, and I'll see you next time!

